<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.13.2: Creating Tables from Verbal Descriptions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00286</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.13.2: Creating Tables from Verbal Descriptions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>dfee20b0-c12d-458a-838c-67a0d2e78d99</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Creating a Table of Values</title>
<para>For each situation in numbers 1 – 3, create a table of values with at least five columns to represent the situation.</para>

<!--Q#1-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Julio works at a clothing store and makes $14 per hour. </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
    <thead>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Number of Hours</entry>
        <entry>0</entry>
        <entry>1</entry>
        <entry>2</entry>
        <entry>3</entry>
        <entry>4</entry>
        <entry>5</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Amount Earned</entry>
        <entry>0</entry>
        <entry>14</entry>
        <entry>28</entry>
        <entry>42</entry>
        <entry>56</entry>
        <entry>70</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> Jake had cavities at his last dentist visit. The dentist told him to brush his teeth for two minutes each time he brushes. </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
    <thead>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Amount Earned</entry>
        <entry>1</entry>
        <entry>2</entry>
        <entry>3</entry>
        <entry>4</entry>
        <entry>5</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Total Number of Minutes Brushed</entry>
        <entry>2</entry>
        <entry>4</entry>
        <entry>6</entry>
        <entry>8</entry>
        <entry>10</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#3-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> For a fundraiser, Celia ran 5 miles on Monday (day 0) and then 3 miles every day after that. </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
    <thead>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
        <entry>0</entry>
        <entry>1</entry>
        <entry>2</entry>
        <entry>3</entry>
        <entry>4</entry>
        <entry>5</entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
        <entry>5</entry>
        <entry>8</entry>
        <entry>11</entry>
        <entry>14</entry>
        <entry>17</entry>
        <entry>20</entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<title>Using a Table of Values to Write Equations</title>
<para>Table of values can be used to write equations. The tables from <emphasis>Creating a Table of Values</emphasis> all represent linear equations. </para>
<para>For 4 - 8, revisit the table from question 1 and write an equation to represent the table of values. Notice that columns for the \(x\) and \(y\) values are added. </para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry>1</entry>
      <entry>2</entry>
      <entry>3</entry>
      <entry>4</entry>
      <entry>5</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
      <entry>0</entry>
      <entry>14</entry>
      <entry>28</entry>
      <entry>42</entry>
      <entry>56</entry>
      <entry>70</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="cf17ccab-8092-4240-ac79-9f8bab96fa7e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0"><!--Q#4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="7a5095fe-59e3-4bcf-9f11-a5bdfa8e1c46" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="0">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the starting value (when \(x = 0\), what does \(y\) equal)? </para>
      <para>Enter your answer here.</para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(y = 0\)</para>
    </solution>
    </exercise>
  <!--END QUESTION.-->
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
  <solution>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
  </div>
</div>

<!--Q#5-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> How would you describe this value on the graph? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(y\)-intercept</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#6-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> What is the rate of change, or the change between the \(y\)-values over the change between the \(x\)-values? 
        <div class="os-raise-d-flex-nowrap os-raise-justify-content-center">
          <iframe><iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/nZiRu4PpXDo?si=5Rg6NDyzCgjfNHwO;&amp;rel=0" title="YouTube video player"/></iframe>
        </div>
      </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(\frac{14}{1}\) or 14</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#7-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> How would you describe this value on the graph? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>slope</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#8-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Using the information in questions 4 – 7, what would the equation be for the values represented by the table? Use slope-intercept form. </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(y= 14x +0\) or \(y = 14x\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#9-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write an equation from the table of values created in question 2 of <emphasis>Creating a Table of Values</emphasis>.</para>
    <para>Hint: (Work backward to find the value where \(x = 0\) using the pattern set in the table of values).</para>
    <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
      <thead>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
          <entry>0</entry>
          <entry>1</entry>
          <entry>2</entry>
          <entry>3</entry>
          <entry>4</entry>
          <entry>5</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
          <entry>?</entry>
          <entry>2</entry>
          <entry>4</entry>
          <entry>6</entry>
          <entry>8</entry>
          <entry>10</entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(y = 2x\) (note: subtract the top row by 1 and the bottom row by 2 to go back to where \(x = 0\) for the \(y\)-intercept).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->


<!--Q#10-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Write an equation from the table of values created in question 3 of <emphasis>Creating a Table of Values</emphasis></para>
    <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
      <thead>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(x\)</entry>
          <entry>0</entry>
          <entry>1</entry>
          <entry>2</entry>
          <entry>3</entry>
          <entry>4</entry>
          <entry>5</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">\(y\)</entry>
          <entry>?</entry>
          <entry>2</entry>
          <entry>4</entry>
          <entry>6</entry>
          <entry>8</entry>
          <entry>10</entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(y = 3x +5\)</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

